    stem: `Surya Lighting, an imagined firm, had ${rs(5500)} in cash and a bank overdraft of ${rs(9000)} on 1 March 2028. Prepare its triple column cash book for March 2028 and balance it. 1 Mar: cash sales ${rs(14000)}. 3 Mar: received a cheque for ${rs(16000)} from Pankaj Ahuja and kept it in the office. 5 Mar: paid wages ${rs(4800)} in cash. 7 Mar: paid Pankaj Ahuja's cheque into the bank. 9 Mar: paid Gopal and Sons ${rs(19400)} by cheque, after discount of ${rs(600)}. 12 Mar: received ${rs(8820)} in cash from Zubin Ali, after allowing discount of ${rs(180)}. 15 Mar: deposited ${rs(9000)} of cash into the bank. 19 Mar: paid electricity ${rs(2750)} by cheque. 22 Mar: paid rent ${rs(6000)} in cash. 28 Mar: the bank charged interest of ${rs(540)} on the overdraft.`,
